d\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2d816e3d8eb7986a436a9aa1552497aa5eacd5095b79d3860f057e49419254a6","event_uuid":"70232d83-8b26-4b93-afc2-b5e5935bccf6","position":{"commit_sha":"5c19a360db8f83dc5facfe4a6fd7567f2f9c129f","position":"1788485900966688001-70232d83-8b26-4b93-afc2-b5e5935bccf6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"18ea01b75d336144b5ff6dea6b67ed2cce518334d4de7949e865d4c090e5a346","event_uuid":"d716623a-49e8-4ea8-9681-140c43809d1e","position":{"commit_sha":"22d341097ee2616abd954e14fbec7d91aadf0bb5","position":"1788485923565391001-d716623a-49e8-4ea8-9681-140c43809d1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-b35a-abf6. Plan was revised to specify marked generated taxonomy block, canonical type/status source, drift-check behavior, and relationship-prose preservation; plan-review is certified at 972fa4dd932d85cd208f7a8c619d955c83269216.","timestamp":1788469709702472851},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out TDD implementation reached local validation except the full non-integration suite hit an unrelated existing failure outside this ticket's file_impact: `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head` fails because `git rev-parse refs/heads/tickets` in the test's temporary remote exits 128. Focused taxonomy oracle, taxonomy --check, lint, and typecheck pass; mutation seeded by replacing `identity` in the generated block returns RED as expected. Per protocol I am not forcing or editing outside scope.","timestamp":1788474050765763666}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788313837563627001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"73d25a99-417e-4698-be16-0f6cf84ccdd9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ca9f-392b-11a7-4489"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`docs/ticket-model.md:12` currently hand-maintains the ticket taxonomy and says there are five ticket types/statuses. The canonical vocabulary in `src/rebar/types.py:21-23` now defines seven statuses (`idea`, `open`, `in_progress`, `blocked`, `closed`, `archived`, `deleted`) and seven ticket types (`bug`, `epic`, `story`, `task`, `session_log`, `code_review`, `identity`). The relationship prose below that intro is already current, so this ticket is limited to eliminating taxonomy drift while preserving the hand-maintained relationship documentation.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a deterministic generator/checker at `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py` that imports the canonical `TicketType` and `TicketStatus` literals from `src/rebar/types.py`, renders only a clearly marked taxonomy block in `docs/ticket-model.md`, and leaves all prose outside the markers byte-for-byte unchanged. The generated block will replace the stale introductory taxonomy sentence with tables/lists for the canonical type and status vocabularies plus a short note that the relationship sections remain hand-maintained. The script will support a write mode to regenerate the block and a check mode that exits non-zero when `docs/ticket-model.md` is stale after a vocabulary change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/types.py`: read-only source of truth for `TicketType`/`TicketStatus`; tests may monkeypatch or copy a fixture to simulate a vocabulary addition, but the production vocabulary is not changed by this ticket.\n- `docs/ticket-model.md`: receives one marked generated taxonomy section; all relationship/hierarchy/link/tag prose outside the markers must be preserved.\n- `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`: new deterministic generator and drift checker with stable ordering from the canonical literal definitions.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`: held-out oracle coverage for generation, stale-output detection, and simulated source-vocabulary drift.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out TDD will start with unit tests for the generator/checker rather than editing production code first. The oracle covers:\n\n1. Rendering includes all seven live ticket types and all seven live statuses from `src/rebar/types.py:21-23`.\n2. Running the generator against `docs/ticket-model.md` preserves relationship prose outside the marked taxonomy block.\n3. A deliberately stale generated block makes check mode fail and report that regeneration is required.\n4. A deliberate source-vocabulary addition in a copied/monkeypatched `types.py` fixture makes check mode fail when the documentation was not regenerated.\n5. Re-running generation is deterministic/idempotent: a second run produces no diff.\n\nValidation commands: the focused pytest for `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`, the documented script check mode, then the ticket's verify commands (`make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test` when required by the ticket gate).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `docs/ticket-model.md` contains a marked generated taxonomy section whose type/status content is derived from the canonical `TicketType` and `TicketStatus` literals in `src/rebar/types.py:21-23`.\n- [x] The generated taxonomy lists all seven current ticket types and all seven current statuses, including `code_review`, `identity`, `archived`, and `deleted`; verified by `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`.\n- [x] Hand-maintained relationship, hierarchy, link, and tag prose outside the generated taxonomy markers is unchanged by regeneration; verified by a preservation test.\n- [x] `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py --check` exits non-zero for both a deliberately stale generated block and a simulated source-vocabulary addition without regeneration.\n- [x] Generation is deterministic/idempotent: running the write mode twice leaves `docs/ticket-model.md` unchanged on the second run.\n- [x] The focused generator tests pass and the ticket verify commands pass before the Gerrit change is submitted.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"canonical ticket type/status vocabulary"},{"path":"docs/ticket-model.md","reason":"receive marked generated taxonomy section"},{"path":"scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py","reason":"new deterministic taxonomy generator and drift checker"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py","reason":"verify generation and stale-output detection"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","ca9f-392b-11a7-4489"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"70232d83-8b26-4b93-afc2-b5e5935bccf6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","documentation","schema","rp23"],"ticket_id":"b35a-abf6-02fd-4b31","ticket_type":"story","title":"Generate ticket taxonomy documentation from the canonical schema","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py","dd_id":"focused-pytest","dd_text":"Focused generator/checker tests"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py --check","dd_id":"taxonomy-check","dd_text":"Generated taxonomy drift check"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint","dd_id":"lint","dd_text":"Repository lint gate"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck","dd_id":"typecheck","dd_text":"Repository typecheck gate"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test","dd_id":"test","dd_text":"Repository test gate"}]},"source_event_uuids":["83f0f6fb-db0a-47f1-80cc-75a1035c0d11","7eabcb85-78a1-494e-98b9-a1a77108e428","f900800d-ac5c-4777-9db3-b3f5e7c11bf4","91d92ed8-16ae-4889-a352-ef3e2822516e","7a66bdc0-43e7-4f7a-b83c-970cb863e127","5d773289-c80e-4d56-954d-998151ba4d66","c64f5151-bacd-4251-a722-87cc8972b44f","73d25a99-417e-4698-be16-0f6cf84ccdd9","a67f229f-3498-4ed4-8bca-f5c8488987a3","cbab77ea-ed36-46b9-820a-c32f11c320d8","70232d83-8b26-4b93-afc2-b5e5935bccf6","d716623a-49e8-4ea8-9681-140c43809d1e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788491289945621001,"uuid":"b23efc66-1a37-48e7-ac06-b54b30c06944"}